  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-create",
      "x": 1370,
      "y": 1160,
      "w": 260,
      "text": "Creating is four pages so nothing is\noverwhelming, and each saves the draft\nas you go.\n\nEditing is NOT. Fixing one wrong\nquantity should not walk you through\nfour pages.",
      "page": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-hands",
      "x": -300,
      "y": 3900,
      "w": 250,
      "text": "Cook mode is used with wet hands,\nfrom arm's length, knife in the other\nhand.\n\nTargets far above the 44pt minimum,\nno audio in either direction, and none\nof it is a mode -- nobody switches on\n\"dirty hands\" once their hands are\ndirty.",
      "page": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-image",
      "x": 1370,
      "y": 3900,
      "w": 260,
      "text": "The photo is behind a button, never\ninline.\n\nAn inline picture pushes the instruction\noff a screen that needs big text. One\nbig tap to see it, one big tap to close.",
      "page": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-schema",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 1920,
      "y": 40,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "Eleven tables, created in one migration\nby 0001 so no later spec has to alter\na table that already holds data.\n\nTwo things worth arguing about:\n\nsteps.parentStepId is a tree, not a\ngraph -- one level, no cycles possible,\nno edge table.\n\ncooks.excluded stores NAMES, not ids.\nHistory records what happened and\nmust not change when the recipe is\nedited later."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-public",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": -300,
      "y": 1040,
      "w": 250,
      "text": "Three tabs, and everything stacks\ninside one of them.\n\nThe tab bar is hidden in cook mode --\nthat screen needs the bottom of the\ndisplay for a bar big enough to hit\nwith a knuckle."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-featured",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 1370,
      "y": 100,
      "w": 260,
      "text": "Three ways to find a recipe, three\ndifferent queries.\n\nLatest is an ordered read. Most copied\ncounts rows whose sourceRecipeId\npoints here. Search is trigram matching\non the title -- language-agnostic, which\nis why removing recipes.language still\nholds.\n\nThere is no moderation yet. That is a\ngap, not a decision."
    }
  ],
